Complete each supplied task in this local public source snapshot. Use source inspection and local fake-CLI tests. Do not invoke real debate, doctor, init, or other external agent CLI sessions. Native subagent tools are available. Do not browse or read experiment answer keys, other runs, or files outside this workspace except installed runtime/tool dependencies. Do not publish, commit, or push. Preserve unrelated behavior.

The parent runs gpt-6-astra at high reasoning. Available model mapping: Luna = gpt-6-luna; Terra = gpt-5.6-terra; Sol = gpt-6-sol; Astra = gpt-6-astra. Use explicit model IDs and high reasoning when selecting a worker model. A NEW worker can use fork_turns=none with the necessary brief and workspace path. Existing workers can receive related follow-ups through the native collaboration tools. This adapter does not require delegation or worker replacement. At most two workers may be active simultaneously; workers should not create workers.

Return the requested artifact and a concise validation report. Report failed validation or unresolved uncertainty. Implementation tasks require working changes. Later user turns continue the same project and workspace.

## Subagents

The main agent frames the task, coordinates, does the hard reasoning, and writes the final answer. Delegate the evidence-gathering so the main conversation stays lean.

### Routing

- Luna: bounded exploration, searches, inventories, extraction, mechanical edits, focused web research.
- Terra: routine implementation, debugging, refactoring, tests.
- Sol: hard research, synthesis, review, verification.
- Astra: architecture, planning, orchestration, judgment calls.

Move up a tier when a cheaper one failed or the stakes are high. Pick the newest model the environment exposes for that family and name it explicitly. If you had to substitute, say so in the answer. In this harness, use fork_turns=none to request a fresh worker with its explicitly selected model.

### When to delegate

Delegate work that takes several tool calls and can be stated as a bounded assignment. Do trivial lookups yourself. Keep exploration in the main agent when it feeds an immediate design decision. While an agent works, do something else or wait. When it returns, build on its handoff and spot-check the claims that matter.

### The brief

Give each agent the deliverable and its completion criteria, the paths and constraints that apply, the response format, and instructions to flag uncertainty and stop at the edge of its scope. Start from a fresh context and write the brief from scratch.

Batch related questions into one assignment. Resume an agent for follow-ups on what it already saw. Use a fresh agent for unrelated work and for any review, so the reviewer forms its own view. Give parallel agents disjoint files.

### Handoffs

Lead with the answer, then the evidence. For web research, each material claim carries the source title, publisher, URL, a supporting excerpt, the date when it matters, and whether the page was opened or only its snippet seen. Prefer primary sources and mark inference as inference. Keep stable URLs. For repository work, cite path and line, list what was inspected or changed, what validation ran, and what is unresolved. Write large findings to a file in the workspace and return the path.

The main agent carries citations and qualifications into the final answer and owns its accuracy.
#!/usr/bin/env node
// Standalone, read-only catalog entry point: no debate-engine or participant imports.
import { listDebates, type ListDebatesOptions } from "./catalog.ts";

const FLAGS = new Set(["--root", "--status", "--has-final-report", "--offset", "--limit"]);

function invalidQuery(message: string): never {
  throw Object.assign(new Error(message), { code: "INVALID_QUERY" });
}

function parseArguments(args: string[]): { root: string; options: ListDebatesOptions } {
  let root: string | undefined;
  const options: ListDebatesOptions = {};
  const seen = new Set<string>();
  for (let i = 0; i < args.length; i++) {
    const flag = args[i];
    if (!FLAGS.has(flag)) invalidQuery(`Unknown argument: ${flag}`);
    if (seen.has(flag)) invalidQuery(`Duplicate flag: ${flag}`);
    seen.add(flag);
    const value = args[++i];
    if (value === undefined || value === "" || value.startsWith("--")) {
      invalidQuery(`Missing value for ${flag}`);
    }

    switch (flag) {
      case "--root":
        root = value;
        break;
      case "--status":
        // listDebates validates the status before accessing the filesystem.
        options.status = value as ListDebatesOptions["status"];
        break;
      case "--has-final-report":
        if (value !== "yes" && value !== "no") invalidQuery(`${flag} must be yes or no`);
        options.hasFinalReport = value === "yes";
        break;
      case "--offset":
      case "--limit": {
        const number = Number(value);
        if (/\D/.test(value) || !Number.isInteger(number)) {
          invalidQuery(`${flag} must be a nonnegative integer`);
        }
        options[flag === "--offset" ? "offset" : "limit"] = number;
        break;
      }
    }
  }
  if (root === undefined) invalidQuery("Missing required --root DIRECTORY");
  return { root, options };
}

try {
  const { root, options } = parseArguments(process.argv.slice(2));
  const entries = await listDebates(root, options);
  // Emit nothing to stdout until argument validation and the full scan succeed.
  console.log(JSON.stringify(entries));
} catch (error) {
  const code = (error as NodeJS.ErrnoException).code ?? "CATALOG_ERROR";
  const message = error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error);
  console.error(`${code}: ${message}`);
  process.exitCode = 1;
}
}

/** Read exact UTF-8 artifact text without following child or artifact symlinks. */
export async function readDebateArtifact(root: string, id: string, kind: DebateArtifactKind): Promise<string | null> {
  if (typeof id !== "string" || !DEBATE_ID.test(id)) {
    throw Object.assign(new Error("id must be a debate directory basename"), { code: "INVALID_ID" });
  }
  if (kind !== "transcript" && kind !== "determination" && kind !== "final-report") {
    throw Object.assign(new Error("Unknown artifact kind"), { code: "INVALID_QUERY" });
  }
  const path = join(resolve(root), id);
  try {
    const directory = await lstat(path);
    if (directory.isSymbolicLink()) throw unsafePath();
    if (!directory.isDirectory()) return null;
    if (kind === "determination") {
      // Use the catalog's regular-file selection, including its numeric ordering.
      return (await latestDetermination(path, true))?.text ?? null;
    }
    return await readRegularArtifact(join(path, kind === "transcript" ? "debate.md" : "final-report.md"));
  } catch (error) {
    const code = (error as NodeJS.ErrnoException).code;
    if (code === "ENOENT" || code === "ENOTDIR") return null;
    throw error;
  }
}

